{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Artaxerxes king of kings</b> — Now it tells that the king sent two letters: one to every volunteer to go up, and one to all the treasurers, to give their needs." "<b>Gamir</b> — It is explained in two ways. The first: that gamir is like the translation of כליל תכלת, and it is a hint to all Israel who volunteer to go up, and to מ\"ד for Ezra, a servant under three, and likewise the meaning: for Ezra and for gamur." "<b>And as for</b> — He sent to inform them of his intent by the hand of Ezra." "Another interpretation: gamir — an adjective from the matter of gemara, gemur, and this is a hint to Ezra." "<b>Book of the law</b> — For he is gamir and knows the knowledge of his Elohim, and it will serve as מ\"ד for Ezra in place of two." "<b>And as for</b> — A collective name for the nations across the river."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:10.454772705Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}